Subject: [PATCH] mmc: queue SDIO interrupt work on system_highpri_wq (#43)

On this board the C6's SDIO interrupt is serviced from
host->sdio_irq_work, which sdio_signal_irq() puts on the normal system
workqueue.  Under CPU load that work waits a tick or more behind
CPU-bound tasks while it is the first hop of every RX packet; the #43
debug build measured the full signal -> read_packet() path at mostly
under 1 ms once the work ran, so the queue is the delay, not the work.
system_highpri_wq runs it ahead of normal-priority work, same as the
elevated RX workqueue and TX thread on the driver side.

---
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/sdio_irq.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/sdio_irq.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@
 void sdio_signal_irq(struct mmc_host *host)
 {
 	host->sdio_irq_pending = true;
-	schedule_work(&host->sdio_irq_work);
+	queue_work(system_highpri_wq, &host->sdio_irq_work);
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(sdio_signal_irq);
 
